msgstr "电源已经接通。继电器在走廊更深处。"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: WOLF thanks the engineer for telling him the relay's risk. Avoid a past tense that shows the engineer's gender ("you told me"). Arm the breaker: 合上断路器, the everyday Chinese for switching a breaker on.
#. i18n: story speaker=WOLF engineer=you
#: scripts/main.gd:2640
msgid "Thank you for telling me. I'll take the relay. Arm the breaker."
msgstr "谢谢你告诉我。继电器交给我。去合上断路器。"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=WOLF
#: scripts/main.gd:2644
msgid "No. I won't take that risk blind. Use the manual bypass."
msgstr "不。我不会盲目冒这个险。用手动旁路。"

# machine-translated by Claude (Anthropic), unreviewed
#. TRANSLATORS: i18n: story speaker=narrator
#: scripts/main.gd:2657
msgid "The relay is dark. Arm the breaker first."
msgstr "继电器没有电。先合上断路器。"

